@startuml error-classes
title viscera — error types

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
hide circle
hide empty members

package "viscera" as api {
  enum ErrorDomain {
    Core
  }

  class ErrorCode <<value>> {
    +domain: ErrorDomain
    +value: uint16
    +operator==(ErrorCode, ErrorCode)
  }

  class Error {
    +Error(code, where = current())
    +Error(code, format, args...)
    +withContext(format, args...): Error
    +wrap(newCode, format, args...): Error
    +code(): ErrorCode
    +description(): string_view
    +is(code): bool
    +message(): string_view
    +location(): source_location
    +cause(): const Error*
    --
    -m_code: ErrorCode
    -m_description: string_view
    -m_location: source_location
    -m_node: shared_ptr~const Node~
  }

  class "Result~T~" as Result <<alias>> {
    std::expected~T, Error~
  }

  class "fmt::formatter~Error~" as Formatter {
    +parse(context)
    +format(error, context)
    --
    does not mutate
    no temporary std::string
    {fmt} exceptions become a fallback
    at most kMaxErrorFormatFrames (8)
  }

  class "fail(...)" as Fail <<function>> {
    +fail(code, where = current()): unexpected~Error~
    +fail(code, format, args...): unexpected~Error~
  }
}

package "viscera::detail" as detail {
  class Node <<immutable>> {
    +message: string
    +cause: Error
  }
}

ErrorCode --> ErrorDomain
Error *-- ErrorCode
Error o-- Node : null when code-only
Node --> Error : cause
Result --> Error : unexpected alternative
Formatter ..> Error
Fail ..> Error : builds

note bottom of Error
  is() compares the top-level ErrorCode only.
  location() is this frame and is always present.
  The rendered line's parenthetical location is the
  root origin, unless formatting hit the 8-frame cap.
  A code-only Error does not allocate.
end note

note bottom of ErrorDomain
  v1 enumerator: Core.
  Platform, Io, Asset, Render, Audio,
  Input, and Game are reserved names.
  They are not enumerators until that
  owner's first error enum is added.
end note

@enduml
